              "text": "নারকেল (nārkel) goes back to Sanskrit nārikela, \"coconut palm and fruit\". CDIAL gives no Bengali form under that entry, but it lists Oriya naṛhera and naṛiā, \"coconut\", the forms nearest to Bengali (CDIAL 7075). CDIAL reports Bloch's view that nārikela is a Dravidian compound."
